>
  <p>Nuvellum publishes reporting, analysis, explainers, opinion, reviews and cultural coverage with clear labels, disciplined sourcing and a visual language designed to feel considered rather than disposable.</p>
  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <p>News reporting, analysis, explainers, opinion, reviews and cultural coverage are treated as distinct formats. Readers should be able to tell what kind of work they are entering before the first paragraph does.</p>
  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Published reporting is expected to remain traceable to its sources. Higher-risk material is held to an additional verification step before publication, while material factual corrections are surfaced when a change affects what a reader should understand.</p>
  <h2>How we use technology</h2>
  <p>Nuvellum uses software and automation to assist research, drafting, verification, publishing, distribution and presentation. Those systems are tools within the editorial process; they do not change the publication’s standards or remove accountability for what appears on the site.</p>
  <span slot="aside">Beyond the headline means more than adding length. Nuvellum is built around context, clear distinctions between fact and opinion, and reporting that helps readers understand why a story matters.</span>
</InstitutionalPage>
